# Delegates human sign-in to the reverse proxy: the atlas-gate forwardAuth
# middleware already requires Authelia sign-in with a second factor before
# a request ever reaches this container, and returns the signed-in
# identity as these exact header names (roles/authelia/templates/
# traefik-authelia.yml.j2's authResponseHeaders). SonarQube trusts them
# and provisions the user just-in-time under their own identity — no
# separate SonarQube-local account or password, consistent with "no
# self-service account creation" everywhere else in Atlas.
#
# Verified against SonarQube Community Build's own docs (instance-
# administration/authentication/http-header): generic OpenID Connect is
# NOT available in Community Build, but HTTP header trust auth is, and
# it is exactly what Authelia's forwardAuth already produces.
#
# Traefik strips any client-supplied copy of these headers before this
# point (roles/sonarqube/templates/traefik-sonarqube.yml.j2), so a
# request can only carry them if the gate itself set them.
sonar.web.sso.enable=true
sonar.web.sso.loginHeader=Remote-User
sonar.web.sso.nameHeader=Remote-Name
sonar.web.sso.emailHeader=Remote-Email
sonar.web.sso.groupsHeader=Remote-Groups
